# Hand-written from RFC 9051 until a recorded iCloud session replaces it
# (bud mail-mcp --record, R7 slice 4). C: is what bud must send, S: what
# the server answers; {#} in an S: line is a literal made of the L: lines
# after it, each ending in CRLF, and the next S: line finishes the response
S: * OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 SASL-IR AUTH=PLAIN] IMAP4 service ready
C: a1 LOGIN "someone@example.com" "app-pass"
S: a1 OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 UIDPLUS MOVE IDLE ESEARCH] user logged in
C: a2 LIST "" "*"
S: * LIST (\HasNoChildren) "/" "Sent Messages"
S: * LIST (\HasNoChildren \Trash) "/" "Deleted Messages"
S: * LIST (\HasChildren) "/" Archive
S: * LIST (\HasNoChildren) "/" "Archive/Caf&AOk-"
S: * LIST (\Noselect \HasChildren) "/" Notes
S: * LIST (\HasNoChildren) "/" "INBOX"
S: a2 OK LIST completed
C: a3 STATUS "INBOX" (MESSAGES UNSEEN UIDNEXT UIDVALIDITY)
S: * STATUS "INBOX" (MESSAGES 3 UNSEEN 1 UIDNEXT 42 UIDVALIDITY 1700000000)
S: a3 OK STATUS completed
C: a4 LOGOUT
S: * BYE IMAP4 server logging out
S: a4 OK LOGOUT completed
